<Page title="Privacy" shortTitle="Privacy and data" kicker="Privacy" description="Critical Minerals uses no tracking, cookies or accounts. The worksheet keeps drafts only in your browser, and only if you choose."
  standfirst="This site does not track you.">
  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>Nothing. There are no analytics, advertising or tracking scripts, no cookies, no accounts and no forms that send information to a server. Fonts are served from this site, not from a third party.</p>
  <p>The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub may keep standard server logs, such as IP addresses, for security and operations under its own privacy statement.</p>
  <h2>The worksheet</h2>
  <p>The community-benefit worksheet runs entirely in your browser. Your answers are not sent anywhere. If you tick "Save a draft in this browser", your answers are stored in your browser's local storage on this device until you delete them. The worksheet has a "Delete saved draft" button. Clearing your browser's site data also removes them. Downloads are created on your device.</p>
  <h2>Third-party calls</h2>
  <p>This site makes <strong>no calls to third parties</strong>. Every page, font, script, image, search index and data file is served from this site. There is no analytics service, cookieless or otherwise. Any future third-party call will be listed here in the same change that adds it.</p>
  <p>Links to sources and organisations take you to other websites only when you choose to follow them. Those sites have their own privacy policies.</p>
  <h2>Speeding up navigation</h2>
  <p>When you press a link to another page on this site, your browser may start fetching that page a moment early (prefetch). It never renders pages you have not opened, and nothing is sent to anyone other than this site.</p>
  <h2>Search</h2>
  <p>Search runs in your browser using an index published with the site. Search terms are not sent to a server.</p>
</Page>
